# Prompt & Rules Change Guide

## Style Guide
This document uses spec-style formatting. Bullet points represent rules or invariants and omit terminal punctuation. Full sentences and explanatory paragraphs use standard punctuation. Capitalized keywords (e.g., MUST, MUST NOT) indicate hard requirements. Formatting choices are intentional and must be preserved unless explicitly changing behavior.

## Purpose
Ensure changes to rules.py and prompts.py preserve agent behavior, invariants, and tool-call schemas.

## Scope
Applies to: rules.py, prompts.py.  
Excludes: refactors unrelated to agent behavior, dependency changes, tool implementation changes.

## Definitions
"Schema": the exact JSON shape expected by adjust_country_projections().  
"Invariant": a rule that must always hold (e.g., values in [0,1], education tertiary = 1 - secondary)  
"Workflow discipline": analyze → adjust (if needed) → next

## Procedure
- Identify module(s) affected: education vs age_gender
- Read the existing rules and system prompt end-to-end before editing
- Decide the change type
  - A) Text-only clarification (no behavior change)
  - B) New constraint / new invariant
  - C) Schema change (HIGH RISK)
- Apply edits with minimal changes

## Mandatory checks (must pass)

### A. Tool-call schema checks
- Education prompt must clearly tell the AI to send adjustments inside an adjustments object; ONLY secondary columns (e.g. secondary_2025, secondary_2026). Example: {"adjustments": {"secondary_2025": 0.55}}. Tertiary is auto-calculated as 1 - secondary; do not send tertiary keys.
- Age_Gender prompt must clearly tell the AI to call adjust_country_projections per country-individual (country + individual required). Adjustments are year → value for that combination. Example: country="Austria", individual="Male_25-34", adjustments={"2024": 0.98, "2025": 0.95}, reason="..."
- Any mention of required parameters must match actual tool signature expectations (country, adjustments, reason; individual required for Age_Gender)

### B. Invariant checks
Education rules MUST include
- Outlier rule (> 1% YoY)
- Tertiary + secondary sum to 1.0
- Adjust secondary only; tertiary = 1 - secondary (auto). Never send tertiary in adjustments.
- Sequential year adjustment: adjust secondary_{adjusted_year-1} first, then secondary_{adjusted_year} relative to the adjusted prior year

Age_Gender rules MUST include
- Outlier rule (> 1% YoY)
- Conservative downward adjustments
- Decrease bigger projection (never increase smaller)

### C. Year scoping checks
- Prompts MUST restrict edits to adjusted_year and adjusted_year-1
- Prompts MUST state historical years are never changed

### D. Workflow checks
- Prompts MUST require one function call per API response (no batching multiple calls)
- Prompts MUST keep explicit loop discipline: analyze → adjust (if needed) → next
- Prompts MUST include “do not stop early” completion requirement
- Prompts MUST explicitly instruct the LLM to IMMEDIATELY call the adjust function when an outlier is detected, before analyzing the next country or combination
- If analysis results include feedback, prompts MUST instruct the LLM to incorporate it into adjustments and reason

## Reporting
When done, report
- What changed (files + key lines)
- Why it changed (behavioral intent)
- Confirmation of schema + invariants preserved
- Any risks or follow-ups

Be thrifty and to the point in your reporting.

If a schema change is requested
- Do not implement partially
- Update prompt text, tool code expectations, and add or adjust tests or validators in the same change set
